# Copy to agent.env (mode 600) and fill in. Nothing here is committed.
#
# Where jobs land. One directory per job, each holding task.md.
VPL_JOBS=/project/va-jobs

# The model. Plain pi providers need no base and no wrapper: leave
# VPL_MODEL_BASE empty and put the provider's own key in the environment.
#   google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite      GEMINI_API_KEY
#   nim/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b   NVIDIA_API_KEY
# A vp key is the shared option: one credit per call, an expiry, usage in the
# vp ledger, and the issuer's provider behind the door.
VPL_MODEL_BASE=
VPL_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite
VPL_MODEL_KEY=

# The vp shape, when the agent should spend a slip instead of a raw key:
# VPL_MODEL_BASE=https://api.terg.hr/vp/v1
# VPL_MODEL=vpl/gemini-3.1-flash-lite
# VPL_MODEL_KEY=vp_REPLACE_ME

# How many times to take a job again after the provider says 429 or 5xx.
VPL_RETRIES=2

# How long one job may run, and how often to look for new jobs.
VPL_TIMEOUT=900000
VPL_POLL=5000
